{"item_id": "dbe-mathematics-g11-p1-2015-nov-3.2.2", "source_id": "dbe-mathematics-g11-p1-2015-nov", "pair_source_id": "dbe-mathematics-g11-p1-2015-nov-memo", "subject": "mathematics", "grade": 12, "language": "en", "track": "core_maths", "kind": "question", "question_ref": "3.2.2", "marks": 4, "topic": "number patterns", "passage": "A linear pattern has a difference of $3$ between consecutive terms and its $20^{\\text{th}}$ term is equal to $64$ (that is $T_{20} = 64$).", "question": "Which term in the pattern will be equal to $3T_5 - 2$?", "memo": "$T_n = a + (n-1)d \\\\ T_{20} = a + 19(3) = 64 \\implies a = 7 \\\\ T_5 = 7 + (4)(3) = 19 \\\\ 3(19) - 2 = 55 \\\\ 55 = 7 + (n-1)(3) \\implies 48 = (n-1)3 \\implies 16 = n-1 \\implies n = 17 \\checkmark$", "final_answer": "17", "needs_review": false, "licence": "DBE copyright - check terms", "attribution": "Department of Basic Education"}
